---
description: Request-validation rules for API route input boundaries
globs: apps/api/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Request Validation

- Run request validation only in route middleware before handler logic.
- Do not parse, validate, or coerce request input inside route handlers.
- Validate `req.params`, `req.query`, and `req.body` as separate inputs.
- Return HTTP 400 for invalid `req.params` before any service call.
- Return HTTP 400 for invalid `req.query` before any service call.
- Return HTTP 400 for invalid `req.body` before any service call.
- Keep request schemas in centralized schema modules.
- Reuse existing schemas; do not define inline schemas in route files.
- Keep validation code scoped to request shape and constraint checks only.
